---
title: "Client protocol — subscribe, fetch, apply ⇒ converge (SPEC §5)"
---
sequenceDiagram
    participant C as chain
    participant W as watcher
    participant F as frontend

    F->>W: 1. subscribe WS /ws
    F->>W: 2. GET /grid

    C-->>W: event e1 (cell 42)
    W-->>F: delta e1 — full cell state
    Note over F: arrives before the grid —<br/>held or applied, either is fine

    W->>F: grid bytes (already include e1)
    Note over F: re-applying e1 is harmless:<br/>the delta EQUALS cell 42's state at head

    C-->>W: event e2 (cell 7)
    W-->>F: delta e2 — full cell state
    Note over F: converged — every cell now byte-for-byte<br/>what /grid would return
